  "description": "The idea a designer reasoned from before inventing the rock-paper-scissors sequence, recorded as its author first stated it. Chess board, chess army, chess setup -- but every piece moves as a rook, and a piece may capture only pieces below it in the usual value order. Nothing outranks the king, so the king can never be captured, so the game has no ending: a deliberately unwinnable ruleset, kept to check that the cheap gates say so.",
